# RTU MTT manuals

The SATEL manuals live only in `docs/vendor/rtu-mtt/` on the developer machine. That directory is gitignored and dockerignored. Do not commit the PDFs, the extracted text, `INDEX.md`, or long quotations. The GitHub repository is public.

Product documents in that folder are RTU MTT 2.2.0. The API handbook is RTU MTT 2.0 (2017). Read `docs/vendor/rtu-mtt/INDEX.md` and `api-2.0.txt` before any RTU API design. Do not invent methods, tables, or URLs.

The handbook describes SOAP only. Prefer WSDL v2 at `https://<host>/service/?wsdl_v2`. WSDL v1 is obsolete there. Object names for a 2.2 switch come from that live WSDL, not from the 2.0 handbook alone.

Phone numbers and CDR files still use the SSH allowlist and file intake. SOAP is not an SSH action. The Settings access check reads `getObjects` once. «Текущие звонки» may also `describeTable` and `selectRowset` on the two transit-call tables, summary pages or the shared module templates. When «Состояние вызова» has `have_lookup`, that page may `getLookup` for that column only. `groups.sync` may `describeTable` and `selectRowset` on «Входящие группы» in «Оборудование», with no `node` header and no `getLookup`. `regs.poll` may `describeTable` and `selectRowset` on «Регистрации (ПКомм)» and «Регистрации (ПУпр)» under «Мониторинг ПКомм», and `getLookup` only for «Состояние» on the ПКомм page when `have_lookup` is set. A lookup failure fails that job. Writes stay forbidden unless a separate task names the operation.
